                About Er. Shubham Mishra </h4>
            <p
                style="font-size:16px; font-family:Arial; line-height:30px; text-align:justify; line-height:30px;color:black;">
                Er. Shubham Mishra is currently serving as an Assistant Professor in the Mechanical Engineering
                Department at Bharat Ratna Babasaheb Bhimrao Ambedkar Rajkiya Engineering College, Pratapgarh,
                affiliated to Dr. A.P.J. Abdul Kalam Technical University Uttar Pradesh, Lucknow, India. Along with his
                academic duties, he is also entrusted with important responsibilities as the In-charge of Horticulture &
                Housekeeping, Deputy In-charge Controller of Examination, and Deputy In-charge Training & Placement at
                the institute.
                He has completed his B.Tech. in Mechanical Engineering from Sri Ram Murti Smarak College of Engineering
                & Technology, Bareilly, and his M.Tech. in Mechanical Engineering from Institute of Engineering &
                Technology (IET), Lucknow and Pursuing Ph.D. Degree from Dr. A.P.J. Abdul Kalam Technical University
                Uttar Pradesh, Lucknow, India. Er. Shubham Mishra has presented and published research papers in
                National Conferences. His academic and research interests include Solar Energy, Thermal Systems, Phase
                Change Materials, and Electric Vehicles.


            </p>


